-- §6.2 T3 at the graph-end drain (`compiler/types/typecheck.mdk`).
--
-- `relay`'s inferred scheme quantifies `a` and carries both `Tweak a Int` and
-- `Tweak a Bool`.  The diagnostics-arm drain routes `relay`'s call goals through
-- `routeUndeterminedTop`, where each reaches exactly one instance
-- (`Tweak Float Int`, `Tweak Float Bool`).  A routing by head tag once minted the
-- goal `Tweak Float` from them, dropping the vector's tail, and reported it
-- `T-AMBIGUOUS-INSTANCE`.  The goals are on a scheme-quantified variable, so they
-- are the caller's: the one instance each reaches is not chosen for it.
--
-- SPEC ANSWER, hand-derived: `relay`'s goals belong to its callers; `main` calls it at
-- `Float`, where `Tweak Float Int` and `Tweak Float Bool` are each the unique match.
-- `relay 1 2.5` = `value 1 2.5` = `tweak True (tweak 1 (relay 0 2.5))` = 2.5, since
-- both impls return their second argument.  ACCEPT on every verb, printing `2.5`.
--
-- WHAT THIS ROW PINS: `check` must not report `T-AMBIGUOUS-INSTANCE`.  `check`
-- does not render the drain's own verdict; `compiler/types/typecheck_test.mdk`
-- reads it in-process (no route is minted for either quantified goal).
interface Tweak a b where
  tweak : b -> a -> a

impl Tweak Float Int where
  tweak _ x = x

impl Tweak Float Bool where
  tweak _ x = x

value : (Tweak a Int, Tweak a Bool) => Int -> a -> a
value n x = if n == 0 then x else tweak True (tweak 1 (relay (n - 1) x))

relay n x = value n x

main = println (relay 1 (2.5 : Float))
